# Architecture rules (V1–V3, V8, V11, V14)

## V1 — OS logic isolation

Platform-specific code lives only under `go/internal/collector/` with GOOS build tags (`linux`, `darwin`, `windows`).

Do not add shell/process calls to `internal/runtime` or `internal/web`.

## V2 — Collector contract

Every platform implements `collector.Collector`. Shared system metrics use gopsutil in `system.go`.

## V3 — Shell in collector layer only

Shell/process execution belongs in collector implementations, not in the scheduler or HTTP handlers.

## V8 — Configurable schedules

Use env vars (`METRICS_COLLECTION_INTERVAL`, `DOCKER_COLLECTION_INTERVAL`). No hardcoded sleep loops in production code.

## V11 — Graceful degradation

Collector errors return partial payloads or log warnings. Never crash the scheduler on a single failed collection.

## V14 — Tests for new collectors

New or changed collector logic requires unit tests in `go/internal/collector/`.
